1. Plover (derived code, test generators, golden data)
------------------------------------------------------

Upstream:  Plover, the Open Steno Project, https://github.com/openstenoproject/plover
Copyright: Plover's contributors. The file headers read were:
           "Copyright (c) 2010-2011 Joshua Harlan Lifton" (plover/orthography.py)
           and "Copyright (c) 2013 Hesky Fisher" (plover/translation.py),
           each "See LICENSE.txt for details." Other files carry other holders.
License:   GNU GPL version 2 or later. Checked: Plover's LICENSE.txt is the GPL
           version 2 text, and its setup.cfg states `license = GPL-2.0-or-later`
           (both read from the master branch on GitHub). GPL-2.0-or-later code
           may be used under the terms of GPL version 3 or later.

Derived in keymux (ports of Plover's behavior and, for the orthography, of its
rule table; each file's header says what it ports):

  src/steno/translate.rs    plover/translation.py and macros
  src/steno/formatter.rs    plover/formatting.py
  src/steno/action.rs       plover/formatting.py (actions)
  src/steno/meta.rs         plover/meta/*.py and the {...} parser
  src/steno/orthography.rs  plover/orthography.py and ORTHOGRAPHY_RULES of
                            plover/system/english_stenotype.py (the ordered
                            regular-expression rules are Plover's)
  src/steno/rtf.rs          plover/dictionary/rtfcre_parse.py and its tokenizer
  src/steno/keycombo.rs     plover/key_combo.py
  src/steno/numbers.rs, src/steno/layout.rs, src/steno/layouts/qwerty.ron
                            Plover's stroke notation, number keys and its
                            built-in "Keyboard" machine key mapping
  tools/plover-golden/      scripts that import and run Plover to record its
                            output (not needed to build or test keymux)
  src/steno/testdata/*golden*.json, orthography_words.txt,
  plover_golden_words.txt   Plover's outputs recorded by those scripts, and the
                            part of Plover's word list they looked at (see 2)

Plover is run only by the generator scripts, never linked into keymux.

2. american_english_words.txt (Plover's orthography word list)
--------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream:  plover/assets/american_english_words.txt in the Plover repository.
           keymux does not ship it: `keymux steno theory` downloads it from
           Plover's repository into your steno folder. Only a 570-line excerpt
           is committed, as src/steno/testdata/orthography_words.txt.
License:   It lives in Plover's repository, which is GPL-2.0-or-later (see 1).
           The directory has no separate README or license file, and where the
           list was originally compiled from is NOT verified here.

